Expose the AirPlay 2 pairing PIN as a config option

shairport-sync already carries config.airplay_pin all the way into
pair_ap's pair_setup_new(): NULL (the hardcoded default) lets clients
use transient pairing (no code), a value switches pair-setup to the
HomeKit-normal SRP flow and refuses transient - the sender must
prove knowledge of the code. The server's long-term keypair is
derived deterministically from the device id, so a sender that has
paired once reconnects silently forever after; there is no pairing
store to manage. All that is missing upstream is a way to SET the
pin - this adds general.airplay_pin.

To make senders prompt for the code, also advertise SystemPairing
(feature bit 51) via general.airplay_features_or (patch 0002).
strdup is required: shairport frees config.airplay_pin at exit, and
the bare config_lookup_string pointer is owned by libconfig.

Companion to 0001/0002; carried locally by boompi.

--- a/shairport.c	2026-08-06 16:20:00
+++ b/shairport.c	2026-08-09 09:00:00
@@ -605,6 +605,15 @@
       if (config_lookup_string(config.cfg, "general.airplay_features_or", &str)) {
         config.airplay_features |= strtoull(str, NULL, 16);
       }
+
+      /* HomeKit-style pairing code. When set, transient (no-code)
+         pairing is refused and senders must complete SRP pair-setup
+         with this code once per device; reconnects pair-verify
+         silently. Advertise SystemPairing (bit 51) via
+         airplay_features_or so senders show the code prompt. */
+      if (config_lookup_string(config.cfg, "general.airplay_pin", &str)) {
+        config.airplay_pin = strdup(str);
+      }
 #endif
 #ifdef CONFIG_LIBDAEMON
       /* Get the Daemonize setting. */
